 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The damsel of the Isaurian nation\nMade her young husband's love immortalize him:\nTo do that, she with constant inspiration\nHelped the poet to enrich into\nA masterpiece his simple inspiration.\nHe wrote a poem so great indeed\nThat the King was surprised when undone:\nHis skill alone excelled in effect\nAll other forms; but, as he himself\nTold it from his heart, 'tis far beyond\nThis artifice able to realize.'[139c. Self\nRecalls how, much more than at common",
